{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/pulls/6","id":5184040858,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU0OAK88AAAABNP4vmg","html_url":"https://github.com/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/pull/6","diff_url":"https://github.com/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/pull/6.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/pull/6.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/issues/6","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/pulls/6/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/pulls/6/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/issues/6/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/statuses/544a9665755f1fb058b2277b0977af610a7494da","number":6,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Publish the matched-progress confirmation (N7) result","user":{"login":"rafli-hl","id":289911665,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUezcQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289911665?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl","html_url":"https://github.com/rafli-hl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Result: matched-progress confirmation (N7) on six fresh WikiText-103 draws\n\nPublishes the result of the study pre-registered in #5, before its runs. The sealed analysis ran once, by the owner, and its labels, intervals and readings are reported as produced.\n\n| Step | 512 − 768 | Label | Mean and 95% interval, df 5 | Draws < 0 / > 0 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **P1** | 1e-4, matched on training NLL | **REVERSAL_CONFIRMED** | +0.00909 [+0.00400, +0.01417] | 0/6 |\n| **S1** | 1e-4, matched on the gap | **CONFIRMED** | +0.00808 [+0.00487, +0.01130] | 0/6 |\n| **S3** | 1e-4, fixed updates | **CONFIRMED** | −0.00454 [−0.00795, −0.00114] | 6/0 |\n| **S4** | 3e-4, matched on training NLL | **CONFIRMED** | +0.01394 [+0.00893, +0.01896] | 0/6 |\n| **S5** | 3e-4, fixed updates | **CONFIRMED** | +0.01382 [+0.01116, +0.01648] | 0/6 |\n| **S2** | 1e-4, matched on validation NLL | **UNAVAILABLE** | Not read: 3 of 6 draws have a reading | Not read |\n\nNOT_OVERFIT in all four arms. No draw is flagged for saturation.\n\n**The sealed reading of the primary:** \"At 1e-4, p* at 512 at E3 is above p* at 768 read at the training NLL 512 reaches at E3 (REVERSAL_CONFIRMED). At fixed updates at E3 on these draws, 768 is above 512, so on these draws the comparison axis reverses the 512-768 ordering at 1e-4. This does not show a capacity mechanism, and nothing about Jane Street's scale follows. Matching on training loss also removes any faster learning of the wider model, so neither axis is privileged.\"\n\n**What this changes:** the evidence status of final claims 4 and 5 (`reports/adversarial-review-response-note-20261106-01/CLAIMS_4_AND_5_STATUS.md`). The strongest post-hoc claim is now a publicly pre-registered, confirmed result, for widths 512 and 768 at 1e-4, on these draws. `RESPONSE.md` is not edited.\n\n**What it does not show:**\n- **On validation NLL at 1e-4 the reversal is not confirmed:** S2 is not read, and it is not evidence either way.\n- **At 3e-4 the ordering does not reverse:** 512 is above 768 on both axes tested.\n- **The fixed-update half is fragile:** S3's interval spans 0 with m03 or m05 left out.\n- **The epoch boundary is a limitation, not pursued.** Panel p\\* rises most just after an epoch boundary, and P1 compares 512 at the end of an epoch with 768 partway through the next. With 768 read at the higher p\\* of its bracket in every draw, P1 is +0.00702 [+0.00216, +0.01189], 5/6 positive (post hoc). Readouts inside E2.0–E2.25 are future work.\n\n**The checks:**\n- `RESULT_VERIFICATION.json`: PASS, with no mismatch in 2,861 comparisons of the outputs or in 1,456 table cells. The verifier and the frozen layout are included.\n- `ASSISTANT_CHECK.md`: a post-hoc assistant recomputation from `POINTS.csv`, not a sealed result.\n- **Neither reaches p\\*, the per-draw losses, E0 or clipping,** which need the run files that only the sealed analysis read.\n- **The results report's layout is not in #5.** It was frozen later, when the losses already existed. That they were unopened rests on local records and the owner's word.\n\n**Redacted, and not byte-identical:** `reports/natural-text-matched-result-20261105-01/RESULT.md` (1). Each local home-path prefix is replaced with `<LOCAL_USER_HOME>`, as for two earlier files, and `PUBLICATION_TRANSFORMATIONS.json` maps the original and public hashes. `RESULT_VERIFICATION.json` names the local `RESULT.md`'s hash, `ac482f31…`. Every other file is byte-identical to its local source.\n\n**Contents:** `reports/natural-text-matched-result-20261105-01/`; `reports/natural-text-matched-analysis-20261105-01/`; the run verifications, the input check and a claim in `reports/natural-text-matched-run-checks-20261104-01/`; Run M1's status result; the owner's exit receipts in `work/natural-text-matched-activation-m1-20261104-01/` and `-m2-`; the frozen layout, the verifier and the input check's script from `reports/natural-text-matched-analysis-approval-20261105-01/`; two owner decision records; `reports/natural-text-matched-assistant-recompute-20261106-01/`; and the note in `reports/adversarial-review-response-note-20261106-01/`.\n\n**Also changed:** a link in the root `README.md`; 1 row in `PUBLICATION_TRANSFORMATIONS.json`; `NATURAL_TEXT_STUDIES.md` (N7 added to the index, the scope and status sections updated, the pre-registration sentence now names #5), `PUBLICATION_NOTES.md` and `DATA_AVAILABILITY.md` (the N7 additions and the published receipts described); and `PUBLICATION_MANIFEST.csv`, with the rows of those five root files updated in place and the new files appended, CRLF endings kept.\n\n**Not included:** the corpus, the run folders, model states and per-sequence arrays; and the analysis's exit receipt, which holds a personal home path and which `RESULT.md` names by hash.\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01JvfaYmnEddgunH3yg39Yo4)_","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-06T06:42:28Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T06:46:49Z","closed_at":"2026-11-06T06:46:45Z","merged_at":"2026-11-06T06:46:44Z","merge_commit_sha":"4e3baaea1a52772be37c6404490c602e65256209","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"rafli-hl:results/matched-confirmation-20261106","ref":"results/matched-confirmation-20261106","repo":{"id":1396932651,"node_id":"R_kgDOU0OAKw","name":"sequence-weighting-research","full_name":"rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research","owner":{"login":"rafli-hl","id":289911665,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUezcQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289911665?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl","html_url":"https://github.com/rafli-hl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/gists{/gist_id